# NestJS HTTP layer

- One feature = one module under `src/modules/<name>/` with controller + service registered there, not in `AppModule`.
- Constructor injection only. Export providers the feature needs; import `TypeOrmModule.forFeature([...])` in that module.
- HTTP DTOs use `class-validator` + `class-transformer`. Global pipe is `ValidationPipe({ whitelist: true })`.
- Controllers stay thin: validate input, call the service, return the result.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — Express types / wiring in AppModule
import { Request, Response } from 'express';

// ✅ GOOD
import { Body, Controller, Post } from '@nestjs/common';
import { IsString } from 'class-validator';

export class ConvertFileDto {
  @IsString()
  targetFormat: string;
}
```
